\title{Loopvelocity: Loop Velocity Estimation from Single-Cell Hi-C}
\description{
Estimates loop velocity, the time derivative of the chromatin contact state, from single-cell Hi-C. A loop-extrusion kinetic model (one-sided phi(alpha, beta, gamma) and two-sided phi(alpha, theta, gamma) parameterizations) is fitted to contacts in ~50kb windows around TAD boundaries via a steady-state regression or an EM dynamical model, and cell states are extrapolated on embeddings. Provides native readers for cool/mcool/scool, 4DN pairs, and sparse contact matrices, plus insulation-score TAD boundary calling.
